            <h1>A Trusted Islamic Travel Agency in the UK for Hajj and Umrah Services</h1>

<p>Islamic Travel is a Hajj and Umrah travel agency in Stratford, London. We arrange flights, visas, Nusuk permits, hotels near the Haram and transfers for Muslims all over the UK. Every booking with flights is protected under ATOL 12192, held by Travixum Ltd. You can reach our team seven days a week, before you fly and while you are in Makkah and Madinah.</p>

<p>We have been arranging pilgrimages for British Muslims since 2017. More than 10,000 people have travelled with us. Our customers have left over 500 reviews on Trustpilot and our rating is 5 stars. We do not tell people we are the best. We would rather you read the reviews, check our ATOL number, (12192) and come and see our office for yourself.</p>

<h2>Why UK Muslims book with Islamic Travel</h2>

<p>A good Umrah Travel agency needs to give you three things. Your money must be safe. The price must be honest. And someone must answer the phone when things go wrong. Here is how we do all three.</p>

<p><strong>Your money is protected by ATOL</strong>. Every package with flights is covered under ATOL 12192. If we could not provide your trip, the ATOL scheme would refund you or bring you home. You get an ATOL Certificate when you book. You can check our number yourself at caa.co.uk.</p>

<p><strong>No hidden extras</strong>. Every quote lists your flights, your hotels by name with the distance from the Haram, your visa, your transfers, and anything that is not included. The price we quote is the price you pay.</p>

<p><strong>A real office in London</strong>. We are at The Old Dispensary, 30 Romford Road, Stratford, London E15 4BZ. You are welcome to come in, sit down with one of our advisors and plan your trip face to face. We are a registered UK company, not a WhatsApp number.</p>

<p><strong>Help while you are in Saudi Arabia</strong>. You can reach our UK team by phone and WhatsApp for the whole of your trip. If a flight changes or there is a problem with your hotel at 3am, you ring us and we deal with it.</p>

<p><strong>Beat My Quote</strong>. Found the same package cheaper somewhere else? Send us the written quote and we will try to beat it.</p>

<p><strong>Advisors who have been there themselves</strong>. Many of our team have done Umrah and Hajj. When you ask if a hotel really is five minutes from the Haram, you get an answer from someone who has walked it.</p>

<h2>What we offer</h2>

<p><a href="https://www.islamictravel.co.uk/umrah-packages.html"><strong>Umrah packages</strong></a> from the UK Flights, visa, help with your Nusuk permit, hotels in Makkah and Madinah, and transfers, all in one price. 3, 4 and 5-star hotels. 7 to 14 nights. From &pound;549 per person.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.islamictravel.co.uk/cheap-hajj-packages.html"><strong>Hajj packages</strong></a> from the UK Flights, Hajj visa, hotels, the camps at Mina, and guidance through the five days of Hajj. UK places are limited each year, so book early.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.islamictravel.co.uk/umrah-visa.html"><strong>Umrah visa</strong></a> only Booked your own flights and hotels? We can do your Umrah visa and help you register your Nusuk permit. Visas usually come through in a few working days.&nbsp;</p>

<p><a href="https://www.islamictravel.co.uk/halal-holidays.html"><strong>Halal holidays</strong></a> Muslim-friendly resorts in Turkey, the Maldives and elsewhere. Halal food and private pools.</p>

<h2>About Islamic Travel</h2>

<p>Islamic Travel started in 2017 with one aim. To make Hajj and Umrah affordable, safe and simple for Muslims living in the UK. We began as a small London agency. We are now one of the most reviewed pilgrimage agencies in the country, with customers from London to Glasgow.</p>

<p>Our company name is Travixum Ltd, company number 13555073, and we trade as Islamic Travel. We are registered in England and Wales and we hold ATOL licence 12192. Our advisors have arranged thousands of trips between them. Customers on Trustpilot often mention by name.</p>

<p>We are not the only agency selling Umrah packages in the UK, and we will never push you to book. Our job is to give you clear prices, straight answers and proper financial protection. The decision is yours.</p>

<h2>Umrah from London, Manchester, Birmingham and the rest of the UK</h2>

<p>We arrange flights from every main UK airport. London has the most direct flights to Jeddah and Madinah. Birmingham and Manchester have direct Saudia flights as well as good-value one-stop flights through Istanbul, Doha and Dubai. If you live near Leeds, Glasgow, Edinburgh, Cardiff or Newcastle, we book you a connecting flight on one ticket.</p>

<h2>What our customers say</h2>

<p>Islamic Travel is rated 5 stars on Trustpilot from more than 500 reviews. Three things come up again and again. Honest advice with no pressure to book. Trips that turned out exactly as promised. And help that carried on after people landed in Saudi Arabia.</p>

<h2>How to book</h2>

<p>It takes three steps.</p>

<ol>
	<li><strong>Ask for a quote</strong>. Call 0203-970-4500, message us on WhatsApp, or fill in the Plan Your Own Umrah form. Tell us your dates, your nearest airport, how many of you are travelling, and roughly what you want to spend.</li>
	<li><strong>Confirm your package</strong>. We send you a written quote with every cost and every hotel named. Pay a deposit through our secure, ATOL-protected portal to hold it. You can pay the rest in instalments.</li>
	<li><strong>Travel</strong>. We sort your visa, help you register on Nusuk, and send your full itinerary before you fly. You can reach us for the whole trip.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Is Islamic Travel a trusted Umrah agency?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Yes. We are ATOL protected (ATOL 12192, held by Travixum Ltd, company number 13555073) and registered in England and Wales. We have 500+ reviews on Trustpilot and a 5-star rating. We have arranged Hajj and Umrah for UK Muslims since 2017, from a real office in Stratford, London.</p>

<h3>Is my money safe with Islamic Travel?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Yes. Every package with flights is protected under ATOL 12192. If we could not provide your trip, the ATOL scheme would refund you or bring you home. You get an ATOL Certificate when you book. You can check our licence at caa.co.uk.</p>

<h3>How do I check if an Umrah agency is genuine?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Look up its ATOL number on caa.co.uk and make sure the company name matches. Ask for the ATOL Certificate in writing and check that flights, hotels and transfers are all listed on it. Do not book with anyone who only works through WhatsApp or social media and has no office or licence.</p>

<h3>Where is Islamic Travel based?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Our office is at Suite No.5, The Old Dispensary, 30 Romford Road, Stratford, London E15 4BZ. You can visit us, or call us on 0203-970-4500, WhatsApp or email, seven days a week.</p>

<h3>Which UK airports do you fly from?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>London Heathrow, Gatwick, Stansted and Luton, Manchester, Birmingham, Glasgow, Edinburgh, Leeds Bradford, Newcastle, Cardiff and most other UK airports.</p>

<h3>What is Beat My Quote?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>If another UK agency gives you a written quote for the same package, send it to us and we will try to beat it.</p>

<h3>Can I pay in instalments?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Yes. Most packages can be held with a deposit. You pay the rest in instalments before you travel, through our secure portal.</p>

<h3>Can you just do the Umrah visa?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Yes. If you have booked your own flights and hotels, we can do your Umrah visa and help with your Nusuk permit on its own.</p>

<h3>Do you do Hajj as well as Umrah?&nbsp;</h3>

<p>Yes. We arrange full Hajj packages with flights, Hajj visa, hotels, the camps at Mina, and guidance through the days of Hajj. UK Hajj places are limited each year, so booking early matters.</p>

